-- title:
--   Theorem 6.1 (N) — if $U$ conserves $v$, some $\pi\in G(\hat\pi)$ has $I(\pi) \ge v - \varepsilon$
-- statement:
--   Let $\hat\pi$ be a Markov policy (a countable collection of measurable maps $S\to A$) of a negative dynamic programming problem, $U$ its operator, and $G(\hat\pi)$ the set of Markov policies all of whose decision rules are $\hat\pi$-generated. Suppose $U$ **conserves** $v\in M(S)$, i.e. $Uv\ge v$. Then for every $\varepsilon>0$ there is $\pi\in G(\hat\pi)$ with
--   $$I(\pi) \ \ge\ v - \varepsilon \qquad\text{on } S.$$
--
--   A conserved function is therefore a lower bound, up to $\varepsilon$, for what Markov policies generated by $\hat\pi$ can achieve. This is the basic construction behind Theorem 6.2 and the existence of $(p,\varepsilon)$-optimal Markov policies.
--
--   The paper states this for the discounted (previously known) and negative cases; this item is the negative case. **Formalization Note** "$U$ conserves $v$" (`Conserves`) includes $v\in M(S)$. $G(\hat\pi)$ is expressed with the published predicate `IsGeneratedPlan`. $I(\pi)$ is the return of the Markov plan viewed as a deterministic plan (`MarkovPlan.toPlan`).
-- source:
--   Strauch, Negative Dynamic Programming, Ann. Math. Statist. 37 (1966), p. 881, Theorem 6.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DiscountedDP_Stationary_Model
import Definitions.Def_DiscountedDP_Stationary_Return
import Definitions.Def_DiscountedDP_Stationary_Operators
import Definitions.Def_NegativeDP_OptEq_Model
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped ENNReal
open DiscountedDP.Stationary (Hist Plan MarkovPlan stationary IsGenerated IsGeneratedPlan)

namespace NegativeDP.OptEq

variable {S A : Type*} [MeasurableSpace S] [StandardBorelSpace S] [Nonempty S]
  [MeasurableSpace A] [StandardBorelSpace A] [Nonempty A]

/-- Strauch (1966), Theorem 6.1, p. 881, negative case: if the operator `U` of `π̂` conserves
`v ∈ M(S)` and `ε > 0`, some `π̂`-generated Markov plan `π` has `I(π) ≥ v − ε`. -/
theorem theorem61 (P : NegativeDP.Stationary.Problem S A) (πhat : MarkovPlan S A) (v : S → EReal)
    (hv : Conserves P πhat v) (ε : ℝ) (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ π : MarkovPlan S A, IsGeneratedPlan πhat π ∧
      ∀ s, v s - (ε : EReal) ≤ NegativeDP.Stationary.I P π.toPlan s := by sorry

end NegativeDP.OptEq
